rustls-platform-verifier on powerpc / powerpc64 Darwin (Mac OS X 10.4-10.6): use the WebPKI verifier
(`others.rs`: rustls-webpki + rustls-native-certs) instead of the Security.framework one (`apple.rs`), which
calls SecTrustEvaluateWithError (10.14) and SecTrustSetOCSPResponse (10.9), so every link fails (tlrc 1.13.1).
The security-framework / core-foundation dependencies are dropped there. Root certificates come from
rustls-native-certs 0.8, whose crate patch reads MacPorts' curl-ca-bundle on these targets.

